  "dom_id": "step-q337197",
  "name": "Question 13",
  "problem": "A production analyst records the number of flawed units in sampled batches. The data are summarized below. If $X$ is the number of flawed units in a batch, what is the expected value of $X?$\n\n| Number of Batches | $10$ | $9$ | $6$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Flawed Units | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ |\n\n$\\text{E}[X]=$\n{{field-1}}",
  "worked_solution": "The expected value of a discrete random variable $X$ with probability mass function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]={\\sum }_{x\\in S}x\\cdot f(x).\n$$\n\nWe're given the frequencies of the flawed units, so we can start by computing the corresponding probabilities. The total number of batches is $10+9+6=25,$ so the corresponding probabilities are as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X=0)=f(0) & =\\frac{10}{25} \\\\ P(X=1)=f(1) & =\\frac{9}{25} \\\\ P(X=2)=f(2) & =\\frac{6}{25}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe organize these results in the table below.\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $f(x)$ | $\\frac{10}{25}$ | $\\frac{9}{25}$ | $\\frac{6}{25}$ |\n\nNow, summing up the products of each value of $X$ and its associated probability, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & =0\\cdot f(0)+1\\cdot f(1)+2\\cdot f(2) \\\\  & =0(\\frac{10}{25})+1(\\frac{9}{25})+2(\\frac{6}{25}) \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{25}+\\frac{12}{25} \\\\  & =\\frac{21}{25} \\\\  & =0.84.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
